OL,3,GNEWSAGodmother of rock and roll's city
OL,4,Agig honoured
OL,5,
OL,6,FA unique slice of Manchester's musical
OL,7,Fhistory - when the "Godmother of rock
OL,8,Fand roll" performed live at a city
OL,9,Frailway station - has been
OL,10,Fcommemorated.
OL,12,FThe day Sister Rosetta Tharpe played at
OL,13,Fthe disused station at Whalley Range's
OL,14,FWilbraham Road in May 1964 has been
OL,15,Fmarked with the unveiling of a blue
OL,16,Fplaque.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,410,400,260,160,0,100
PN,40902
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F409A1787216154
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kj 5j js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,,
OL,3,GNEWSAGodmother of rock and roll's city
OL,4,Agig honoured
OL,5,
OL,6,FTharpe, who influenced music legends
OL,7,FChuck Berry, Elvis Presley and Little
OL,8,FRichard among others, was recording a
OL,9,Fshow for Granada TV's Blues and Gospel
OL,10,FTrain, along with greats such as blues
OL,11,Fgiant Muddy Waters.
OL,13,FThe plaque is part of an initiative by
OL,14,Fsocial historian and broadcaster Karen
OL,15,FGabay, to place plaques across
OL,16,FManchester, honouring Black musicians
OL,17,Fwho left a mark on the city.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
